{"Title":"An Act relative to accidental disability and Group 1 emotional distress","BillNumber":"H12","DocketNumber":"HD12","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":null,"Name":"Public Employee Retirement Administration Commission","Type":4,"Details":null,"ResponseDate":"2023-03-06T15:04:14.403"},"Cosponsors":[],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H12/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"So much of the recommendations of the Public Employee Retirement Administration Commission (House, No. 8) as relates to accidental disability and Group 1 emotional distress. Public Service.","DocumentText":"\tParagraph (a) of subdivision (3) of section 7 of chapter 32 of the general laws, as appearing in the 2020 official edition, is hereby amended in line 182 by adding:\r\n\tMembers or beneficiaries filing for benefits under this section or section nine solely on the basis of an emotional disability, may use the official records of his department to establish proof of an injury sustained or a hazard undergone.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J23","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J23"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}